From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:35:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] clutter: position shell text with fractional glyph
 advances

Rounding glyph advances to whole pixels makes letter spacing uneven at
small sizes. Leave metrics unhinted, as GTK 4 does, so Pango places
glyphs at fractional positions.
---
 clutter/clutter/clutter-backend.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/clutter/clutter/clutter-backend.c b/clutter/clutter/clutter-backend.c
index bac8db986669567a5b052e7f6ad7831d1e1aacb6..1d670bd3380644c4b881826b0fa1ed1d37d43ac5 100644
--- a/clutter/clutter/clutter-backend.c
+++ b/clutter/clutter/clutter-backend.c
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@ clutter_backend_init (ClutterBackend *self)
 #ifdef HAVE_FONTS
   self->font_options = cairo_font_options_create ();
   cairo_font_options_set_hint_metrics (self->font_options,
-                                       CAIRO_HINT_METRICS_ON);
+                                       CAIRO_HINT_METRICS_OFF);
   cairo_font_options_set_hint_style (self->font_options,
                                      CAIRO_HINT_STYLE_NONE);
   cairo_font_options_set_subpixel_order (self->font_options,
